@startuml agent-claim-states
' Revision (2026-10-13): accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
title M-DP2: allocation, execution claim and capacity ownership, service slices (draft)
state "agent/1 (dispatcher-owned record; helper owns OS account ledger)" as Agent {
  state "provisioning" as Provisioning
  state "idle" as Idle
  state "running" as Active
  state "retiring" as Retiring
  state "removed" as Removed
  state "failed" as Failed
  [*] --> Provisioning : admitted ordinary provision / operator-signed team bring-up
  Provisioning --> Idle : trusted create + binding confirmed; workplace backend separately gated
  Provisioning --> Retiring : ordinary provisioning failed / operator-signed standing retirement
  Provisioning --> Provisioning : standing failure: reconcile / await operator-signed decision
  Idle --> Active : dispatcher commits execution claim under lock
  Active --> Idle : execution finished; ordinary kept / standing allocation
  Active --> Retiring : ordinary dispatch finished / expiry destruction gate satisfied
  Active --> Retiring : operator-signed standing retirement
  Idle --> Retiring : ordinary retire / expiry destruction gate satisfied
  Idle --> Retiring : operator-signed standing retirement
  Retiring --> Retiring : effects pending / observations unknown or contradictory
  Retiring --> Removed : applicable export recorded or waived; applicable unbind, retire, identity cleanup confirmed
  Retiring --> Failed : failed provision; applicable cleanup confirmed
}
state "run/1 execution claim (dispatcher-owned; enum §4.4)" as Exec {
  state "claimed" as Claimed
  state "launching" as Launching
  state "started" as Started
  state "stopping" as ClaimStopping
  state "absent" as Absent
  [*] --> Claimed : dispatcher writes execution_id + epoch
  Claimed --> Launching : supervisor durable registration before launcher call
  Claimed --> Absent : cancel before launch / no supervisor registration on reconcile
  Launching --> Launching : receipt unknown; cancel waits; never relaunch
  Launching --> Started : launcher receipt known and recorded
  Started --> ClaimStopping : explicit stop (cancel / authorised host_stop) / operator action / exit / incident hard stop
  Started --> ClaimStopping : ordinary execution only: runtime deadline elapsed
  Started --> ClaimStopping : supervisor known absent
  ClaimStopping --> ClaimStopping : receipt missing -> retry same E-stop\nunknown/contradictory -> retain claim
  ClaimStopping --> Absent : latest-receipt fence; quiet-period account-wide absence
}
state "Capacity claim (§9; conceptual ownership, not a stored state enum)" as Capacity {
  state "reserved for owner record\nclaim_id, class, resources, expires_at" as Reserved
  state "owned by execution" as Owned
  state "released after confirmed end/absence" as Released
  [*] --> Reserved : dispatcher admits capacity
  Reserved --> Owned : transfer at start
  Owned --> Owned : unknown process evidence; no release
  Owned --> Released : confirmed end/absence, including cancel/expiry/reconcile
}
note bottom of Agent
  Dispatcher service UID swarma-dispatcher owns persistent agent/run records,
  immutable inputs, effects, journal and capacity claims; local transitions hold lock.
  R-LOCK: intent/in-flight -> unlock call -> lock/fence result; old daemon writers fenced.
  Daemon-owned supervisors run as service UID;
  launcher runs as root until agent UID exec; broker service is unprivileged.
  R-UNTRUSTED: class recorded, workplace untrusted unless operator-admitted to trusted circle; no subscription binding/lease.
  Trusted-circle admission enables donor-side opt-ins only; workplace host boundaries stay.
  Broker owns trusted bindings/leases; launcher writes start receipt; helper confirms stop.
  Ordinary failed provision unbinds if bound and retires if created.
  R-TRANSFER: export recorded or operator waiver before home deletion.
  Retirement: quiesce / declared-key cleanup / home deletion; explicit operator retention only.
  R-TIME: expiry destruction also needs trusted time + monotonic elapsed lifetime.
  R-GEN: fresh random 128-bit generations; restore requires external fence/reverse inventory.
  E-rebind keeps same account; explicit consent/current chains, old removal tombstone.
  Direct operator retirement retains unconfirmed broker-cleanup obligation.
  Standing designation retained; encoding unpublished (§§4.3, 16).
  Standing: no expires_at or lifetime quota; sweep never expires it.
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Every operator act/record from agent sessions refuses; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Only operator-signed retirement or re-creation; no automatic replacement.
  Retirement / re-creation signed-record format is unpublished (§5.4).
  Keeper integration: revoke only registered one-shot identity AFTER retirement;
  standing revocation is operator-only (§14); unknown/refused revocation pending.
end note
note bottom of Exec
  At most one claim per allocation; competing start refuses agent_busy.
  Standing executions have no max_runtime quota or runtime deadline.
  Sweep never stops them for runtime; ordinary executions keep 4 h / 12 h (§3.5).
  Host successor requires lifecycle consent + current owner/chain/start verdict,
  previous claim absent, unchanged plan; same session/op replay never starts twice.
  R-OUTCOME stop continuation keeps same E-stop/arguments, old completed receipt never signals.
  Unknown/contradictory evidence never becomes absent (§4.6).
  Exact launcher-refusal claim transition is unspecified in spec §§4.4, 5.3.
  Supervisor registration/loss are observations, not extra stored claim states.
end note
note bottom of Capacity
  R-CEILINGS: qualified host matrix meets class minimums; no OS-name exclusion.
  Slice 0/helper v0 refuse untrusted; R-EXEC profile required; builds/tests off-host (R-VERIFY).
  R-STANDING: trusted host loop only; untrusted standing placement is workplace.
  R-NET-TOOL/R-RANGE-DENY: zero-egress workplace, provider-only trusted proxy; range rule from v0.
  Web default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only; host boundaries stay.
  No direct/external-http-proxy binding for any platform-host account.
  N15 (2026-10-13): one listener per account_generation, bound to profile_ref; own port only.
  served_policy_digest and service_generation evidence; contract owned by N15.
  R-WATCH v0: affected-account stop, admission hold and observer status; v1 freeze open.
  R-ALLSTOP: direct cuts/stops, receiver launch/create/ingress fence before absence.
  Idle never-launched role: fresh fenced generation absence and full launch coverage; no claim invented.
  Dispatcher-independent stops retain obligations until every part reconciles; recovery explicit (§6).
  Temporary closure: initial refusal / later gated queue; authority/quota never queue.
  Fresh revocation.check at prepare/dequeue/start; revoked/unavailable refuses.
  Prelaunch checks exclude the claim's own resources.
  Claim-expiry transition details and persisted capacity-state enum
  are unspecified in spec §§7.2, 9; expiry alone is not proof of absence.
  Sweep owns ordinary allocation lifetimes; never expires standing allocations.
  Internal daemon sweep every minute; bounded unlocked per-record work.
  Controls stay reachable after prerequisites; confined unknown claims retained.
  Unbounded accounting/shared uncertainty closes node forward admission.
  Capacity-claim expiry is distinct from allocation expiry.
  No sweep running -> status says ordinary lifetimes are unenforced (§7.2).
end note
